[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Explicit native terminal audit qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-NATIVE-TERMINALS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Audit each native bulk MOS terminal and its physical scale
STATEMENT: >>>
An explicitly enabled native bulk MOS audit shall reconstruct D/G/S/B currents
and backward-Euler displacement (Qnew-Qold)/h at each terminal. KCL shall include
all named nodes and ground. Its tolerance shall use the configured absolute
current bound plus relative times the sum of absolute incident currents.
Native power shall sum voltage times signed current at every terminal.
Corrupting an individual clamping-source current shall fail conservation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/native_audit_contracts.rs native_terminal_current_and_dynamic_charge_audits.
Four separate non-ground terminals, two non-unit timesteps and all four current
corruptions. A common-mode translation makes source power nonzero. Gate and
near-zero bulk conduction power are not meaningfully challenged at these biases.
Explicit ignored-test lane requires qualified provider assets.
The manufactured integration state uses the provider as a fixture producer;
it does not independently qualify its model equations. Existing tests/bsim330.rs
retain independent ngspice DC/charge goldens and randomized conservation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-NATIVE-ENERGY-QUAL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve unavailable nonlinear native stored-energy evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Until qualified, a native bulk MOS backward-Euler energy audit shall report
NotChecked with absent discrepancy and tolerance and an explanatory reason.
Passing current conservation shall not imply a qualified energy calculation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: native_terminal_current_and_dynamic_charge_audits checks the
status and absent metrics at two dynamic steps. SOI dynamic charge, other model
families, arbitrary operating points and Linux execution are outside this lane.
<<<
